    packaging only - no changes to TrueNASPlugin.pm from PR #116.

  * APT-managed install / update / rollback (#93, #105): install, update,
    and rollback now shell out to APT against the plugin's own APT repo
    instead of pulling raw .pm files from GitHub. Backup captures the
    installed .deb at backup time so rollback is dpkg-consistent, with
    a cluster-wide opt-in. Source-aware update detection compares against
    the APT candidate on apt-managed nodes (dpkg version ordering, pre-
    release aware) and keeps the GitHub path on raw / dpkg-only nodes;
    a raw cluster pull is refused on non-dpkg nodes. Uninstall runs
    'apt remove' on dpkg-managed packages, and APT install '--reinstall's
    when the package is registered but the .pm file is missing (#105).
