    Cluster parity" plus collect_parity_facts(). Per-node, one local or
    ssh round-trip collects functional facts - iSCSI: node records,
    active sessions, visible LUNs; NVMe: subsystem connected, live
    namespaces - with exact IQN / NQN field matching so sibling targets
    (e.g. ':proxmox-move') do not false-match. Per-node rows plus one
    aggregate row, SKIP on single-node, read-only, non-fatal. 0 LUNs
    while the cluster sees N is CRIT; 0 sessions everywhere is OK
    (login is on-demand); partition nodes are excluded from namespace
    counts; malformed collector output is labeled separately from an
    SSH failure. MTU-match remains deferred per the issue's scope note.
    Verified live 2026-09-29: correctly detected a transient asymmetry
    (pve saw 7 iSCSI LUNs, pvevm1 saw 6) from a just-freed test LUN
    that pve's session still cached.

  * LVM global filter (#4): install.sh offers the global_filter fix
    (with confirmation) after storage config for either transport,
