  * Other sweep items: version reporting trusts 'dpkg-query -W' over
    the plugin's embedded $VERSION (#87), pre-release status derived
    from the dpkg version. A fresh NVMe/TCP install can no longer
    write a literal ':' to tn_discovery_portal; generate_storage_config()
    refuses empty IP / port pairs (#86 part 1). The version picker
    accepts any pre-release suffix ('-alphaN', '-betaN', '-rcN'), not
    just '-debN' (#86 part 2). IPv6 tn_api_host validation and portal
    splitting (#68).

  * install.sh health check preserves the beta6 auth-probe semantics
    (issues #113, #93): auth.me remains the authoritative auth check
    at both call sites; system.info is kept only as a best-effort
    version-display fallback. auth.me is stricter than core.ping (which
    is no_auth_required and would give a false green on a bogus or
    revoked API key) while working for every documented least-privilege
    key. Matches the plugin's own _preflight_check_alloc auth probe.

  * Verified live 2026-09-29 on the 3-node PVE cluster (pve / proxmox2
    / pvevm1, PVE 9.1.1, TrueNAS 25.10.7):
      - live-test-v4 sweep (v3-import, v4-iscsi, v4-nvme, v4-lxc,
        v4-advanced, v4-boot-cluster): 60/60 assertions pass, 0 fail.
      - proxmox-test-runner storage-plugin-validation with 'rootdir'
        enabled on both truenas-storage (iSCSI) and truenas-nvme
        (NVMe/TCP): 19 validated / 0 real failures per transport. The
        1 cluster_migration.pl failure per run was an environmental
        PVE-ticket auth issue in the runner itself (direct 'qm migrate'
        worked), not a plugin regression.
      - LVM filter helper on all 3 nodes: present, executable, syntax
        OK, --status reports correct filter state, --help documented.
      - APT source, apt-cache policy, apt remove + install cleanly:
        plugin runtime remained active through cross-version churn.
      - Cluster parity check detected a real transient asymmetry.

  Closes #4, #21, #60, #68, #86, #87, #93, #105.

