truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.23~beta2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * install.sh: two fixes to the wizard's TrueNAS API write path,
    surfaced by a user report against 2.1.17+deb1 on TrueNAS
    SCALE 25.10.6 / PVE 9.2.11. Both bugs are pre-existing (also
    present in 2.1.17+deb1 and 2.1.23~beta1); only the plugin's
    runtime path was previously fixed for the _NotRequired issue,
    so wizard-driven first-run setup was still exposed.

    - Fix wizard write ops calling a plugin function that does not
      exist. install.sh's tn_api_call_write bash wrapper invoked
      PVE::Storage::Custom::TrueNASPlugin::_api_call_write from an
      embedded Perl block. TrueNASPlugin.pm has never defined a
      _api_call_write; the write-path helper is _api_call_mutate
      (the rename landed in commit d245787 without a corresponding
      install.sh update). Effect: every write op driven by the
      wizard -- pool.dataset.create, iscsi.portal.create,
      iscsi.target.create, nvmet.subsys.create, nvmet.port.create,
      and their delete counterparts -- died inside the embedded
      Perl block instead of reaching TrueNAS. Fix: call
      _api_call_mutate.

    - Fix tn_create_dataset exposing the wizard to the
      _NotRequired audit-logger crash. install.sh's
      tn_create_dataset previously sent only two fields to
      pool.dataset.create: name and type=FILESYSTEM. On
      TrueNAS 25.10.x, every omitted optional field lands in the
      audit-logger as an unresolved _NotRequired sentinel; JSON
      serialization then fails AFTER the create has already
      succeeded server-side. The client sees an error, retries,
      and the retry fails with "dataset already exists" -- leaving
      the successfully-created dataset as an orphan. PR #82 fixed
      this on the plugin runtime side (_tn_dataset_create,
      alloc_image) but the install-time wizard path was still
      exposed. Fix: send all optional fields the FILESYSTEM path
      expects (acltype/aclmode/atime/recordsize/snapdev = INHERIT,
      casesensitivity = SENSITIVE, quota/refquota/reservation/
      refreservation = 0, special_small_block_size = 0) so the
      audit logger has real values to serialize.

  * No plugin runtime changes. TrueNASPlugin.pm bytes are unchanged
    from beta1 except for the VERSION string.

