    response; broker socket missing during systemd restart window;
    could not activate storage during broker-down window) was
    surfaced by the counters but produced no cascading corruption,
    no orphan storms, no deadlocks. Every op that got hit failed
    cleanly and left the next op free to proceed. Fix candidates for
    those signatures (retry-with-bounded-backoff on socket-missing;
    retry-on-EOF for read-only ops) are queued for a later release,
    intentionally not in this beta.

