truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.23~alpha32) unstable; urgency=medium

  * NVMe: LOCKHOLD instrumentation.

    Alpha31 stopped plugin-triggered NVMe reconnects from firing under
    the VM config lock. Kernel logs confirm no more spurious
    "Removing ctrl / new ctrl" events during test runs. But some
    lock-timeout failures still show up in the driver logs at reduced
    frequency, and we can not correlate them to any specific pvedaemon
    action.

    Alpha32 adds level-0 instrumentation at every phase of the two
    code paths that hold the VM config lock while doing NVMe work:
      - _alloc_image_nvme deferred block (runs before cluster_lock_storage
        returns to qm set / qm create, therefore still inside the caller's
        lock hold)
      - _clone_image_nvme deferred block (same pattern for qm clone)
      - activate_volume NVMe branch (runs inside qm start / qm clone
        target's lock hold)

    Each phase log line looks like:
      [TrueNAS] LOCKHOLD alloc_nvme_deferred vmid=105 uuid=<uuid>
                        phase=nvme_rescan elapsed=0.234s

    Grep for LOCKHOLD in journalctl around a lock-timeout event to see
    exactly which phase was still running when the concurrent qm op
    started waiting. Whichever phase most often shows elapsed >5s is
    the actual culprit.

    Pure diagnostic — no behaviour change from alpha31.

