truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.23~alpha31) unstable; urgency=medium

  * NVMe: forbid reconnect in _defer_after_lock pre-warm paths.

    Root cause of the "can't lock file lock-<vmid>.conf - got timeout"
    failures traced by journalctl analysis (2026-08-21 10:33 window on
    pve, VM 121):

      10:32:59  update VM 121 -scsi1        (holds lock, plugin alloc)
      10:33:02  TIMING dataset.create +3.1s
      10:33:05  update VM 121 -tpmstate0    (next holds lock, plugin alloc)
      10:33:08  TIMING dataset.create +3.3s
      10:33:17  kernel: nvme nvme0: Removing ctrl / new ctrl <-- HERE
      10:33:17..30 udev storm: scsi-sg3_id.rules WARNING on ~30 devices
      10:33:35  starting task qmstart:121   (lock wait begins)
      10:33:45  qmstart:121: got timeout    (10s wait exhausted)

    The alloc_image_nvme deferred block (runs under _defer_after_lock,
    which fires WHILE the VM config lock is still held) called
    _nvme_device_for_uuid with allow_reconnect=1. That authorized the
    stale-NGUID reconnect gate at i==10. Under multi-node testing
    (another node just created/destroyed a namespace) NGUID
    contradiction is common, so the gate fires often: kernel does a
    full controller remove+add, udev re-enumerates every namespace on
    the subsystem, plugin's udevadm settle blocks 10-13s waiting for
    the queue to drain -- the entire time still holding the config
    lock. Concurrent qm ops from the test framework on the same VMID
    then time out on the 10s lock wait. VM-config lock timeouts had
    been categorised as harness/PVE issues in earlier reporting;
    corrected: these are plugin-caused.

    Fix: allow_reconnect=0 in both deferred pre-warm calls
    (_alloc_image_nvme deferred at line 5752, _clone_image_nvme
    deferred at line 7782). The deferred block is best-effort; when
    the target device is not yet visible, activate_volume (which runs
    OUTSIDE the config lock, in its own worker, with allow_reconnect=1)
    will do the reconnect cleanly. Recovery isn't lost, just moved to
    a moment the lock isn't held.

