truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.23~alpha26) unstable; urgency=medium

  * NVMe: emergency reconnect after retry budget exhausted.

    Under sustained 3-node concurrent load, ~2 activate_volume calls
    per 250 tests still failed with "Could not locate NVMe device"
    even with alpha24's halfway/last-resort reconnects in place.
    Root cause: those mid-loop reconnect gates never fired because
      - fuser check saw other VMs using the shared subsystem
      - the inline tn_has_uuid check occasionally returned empty
        under TN API load, silently skipping the reconnect body
    Meanwhile the kernel controller was holding stale namespace
    entries whose NGUIDs matched no current TN namespace. Only a
    disconnect+reconnect flushes those stale entries.

    Alpha26 adds a single unconditional emergency reconnect at
    LOOP EXIT — after the 150-iteration budget runs dry, before
    constructing the death error. No fuser check (loop is about to
    fail; brief NVMe I/O pause on other VMs is the lesser evil).
    No tn_has_uuid gate (metadata was queryable enough for the
    failure to be classified). Reconnect, brief 2-second rescan
    retry, and if the target device appears, return it.

    Only gated on allow_reconnect=1 and !reconnect_attempted (some
    earlier gate actually did fire), same as every other reconnect
    site.

