truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.23~alpha7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Narrow-query the iSCSI extent / targetextent hot paths so alloc,
    free, and clone stop paying the full-list cost per operation.
    The previous _tn_extents / _tn_targetextents helpers pulled every
    row on the array back over the wire and cache-invalidated on every
    mutation, so under 3-node concurrent alloc load the cache stayed
    cold and each op serialized 100+ rows just to find or check for
    one. cluster_test_run 2026-08-14 3-node runs surfaced this as
    io_integrity, disk_thin_discard, vm_disk_buses, and
    vm_additional_disk_vtpm hitting the pveproxy 60 s / test-framework
    180 s ceilings while queued behind cluster_lock_storage on the
    other nodes' allocs. New narrow helpers push the filter to
    middlewared using TN's query-filter syntax so the response carries
    only the row(s) actually being asked for:

      _tn_extent_query_by_disk         [[["disk","=",zvol_path]]]
      _tn_extent_query_by_name         [[["name","=",extent_name]]]
      _tn_targetextent_query_by_target_extent
                                       [[["target","=",tid],["extent","=",eid]]]
      _tn_targetextent_query_by_extent [[["extent","=",eid]]]

    Callsites updated in the alloc/free/clone/base-rename flows:
    _resolve_extent_by_disk, _tn_extent_create Fix B recovery,
    _tn_targetextent_create existence + stale-cache recheck,
    _current_lun_for_zname, _alloc_image_iscsi (reuse + Fix B + LUN
    fallback), _free_image_iscsi (main + retry paths + active-LUN
    count), _clone_image_iscsi (all three), _teardown_snapshot_device,
    create_base extent rewire. Read-only inspection paths (pre-flight
    weight-extent check, bulk processor) still use the full-list
    cached readers -- they run once per storage-add, not per-VM.

