truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.23~alpha6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Auto-heal empty iSCSI node-record files at the start of
    _login_target_all_portals. Pre-alpha4 test runs left zero-byte
    /var/lib/iscsi/nodes/<iqn>/<portal>,3260,<tpgt>/default files
    behind (from the -o delete vs -o new race that ~alpha4 stopped
    creating), and `iscsiadm -o new` treats an empty file as an
    existing record and refuses to overwrite it -- so every
    subsequent --login returns "iscsiadm: No records found" and the
    caller busy-loops in PVE's iscsi_login retry harness for minutes.
    New _iscsi_repair_empty_node_records() unlinks the zero-byte
    files (and their empty parent directories) before the -o new
    call so the record gets recreated cleanly. Logs a syslog warning
    listing what it removed so operators can trace the historical
    corruption. ~alpha4 stopped fresh corruption; this heals existing
    corruption in-place so nodes upgraded from pre-alpha4 don't
    require manual /var/lib/iscsi/nodes cleanup.

