truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.23~alpha2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix B (name-conflict recovery) now looks up by extent NAME instead
    of by disk path (test_run6/truenas-2026-08-13 cluster runs still
    hit "iscsi_extent_create.name: Extent name must be unique" despite
    ~alpha1's Fix B). The plugin knows the exact deterministic name it
    submitted; a name lookup is more direct than the by-disk-path grep
    was, and it works even if TN stored the disk field in a form that
    doesn't exact-match what the plugin computes. Reuse only when the
    matched extent's disk field equals the target zvol path; when it
    does NOT match (an unknown extent occupies our hash slot), log the
