    (~60 s). Max R. Carrara's (Proxmox) test_run6 single-node iSCSI
    runs saw the target LUN device appear via the kernel scsi scan
    ~30 s after our previous 20 s timeout gave up, causing
    activate_volume to fail with "Could not locate by-path device for
    LUN N (retries 200)" and cascading VM starts. 60 s covers observed
    latency with headroom. Maximum bumped from 600 to 1200 to keep
    it a valid override.

