truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.23~alpha1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Idempotent iSCSI extent + NVMe namespace create in alloc_image
    (Fix 1). _alloc_image_iscsi and _alloc_image_nvme now check whether
    an extent / namespace already targets the same zvol path and reuse
    its id instead of colliding on the deterministic
    _generate_extent_name hash. Mirrors the reuse pattern the clone
    paths already had.
  * Post-hoc reuse on iSCSI extent name-conflict (Fix B, on top of Fix
    1). New classifier _is_extent_name_conflict_error matches the TN
    uniqueness rejection ("iscsi_extent_create.name: Extent name must
    be unique"). At three iSCSI create sites -- alloc_image,
    clone_image, and the _tn_extent_create helper used by the
    snapshot-expose path -- if the create returns that specific error,
    query iscsi.extent.query by disk path and reuse the extent id if a
    match is found. Catches two failure modes Fix 1's up-front check
    cannot handle: (1) a concurrent path that committed the same
    extent between our pre-check and our create call, and (2) an
    _api_call_mutate retry that fired on a connection failure whose
    first attempt actually committed server-side (the retry then sees
    "name must be unique" from its own prior commit). NVMe/TCP does
    not need Fix B: TN's nvmet uniqueness is per-NSID (server-
    assigned), not on device_path, so the analogous self-race does not
    manifest as a "must be unique" error.
  * Serialize volume_snapshot, volume_snapshot_delete, and
    volume_snapshot_rollback via $class->cluster_lock_storage. PVE
    core's Storage.pm wraps vdisk_alloc / vdisk_free / vdisk_clone /
    vdisk_create_base in cluster_lock_storage (Storage.pm:1090, 1113,
    1170, 1198) but dispatches the three snapshot methods directly
    (Storage.pm:428, 443, 459). Two cluster nodes calling qm snapshot
    on the same volume otherwise raced on the TN pool.snapshot.create
    call, and rollback especially is dangerous unlocked because
    recursive=1 destroys newer snapshots as a side effect. Closes the
    fork()-or-similar-circumventing-locks gap Max R. Carrara (Proxmox)
    flagged in the 2026-08-06 cluster-test writeup.
  * Tests: t/rate-limit/11-alloc-extent-namespace-reuse.t seeds the
    extent-orphan-past-zvol-delete scenario and verifies TN cascade-
    deletes the extent (regression check on the TN behavior our fix
    assumptions depend on). t/rate-limit/12-fix-b-extent-name-conflict.t
    runs a two-tier verification of Fix B: classifier unit tests (no
    TN needed) plus a real-TN uniqueness rejection + recovery lookup.
  * Whether these fixes actually resolve the "Extent name must be
    unique" cascade Max observed in test_run5/truenas-2026-08-06 is
    unproven at ship time; his default tn_debug=0 level gates the
    retry log lines that would otherwise confirm or deny the
    _api_call_mutate self-retry theory. All three fixes ship as
    tolerance / defense-in-depth regardless.
  * An earlier iteration wrapped alloc_image / free_image /
    clone_image / create_base themselves in cluster_lock_storage;
    reverted after PVE core proved to already wrap them and
    cfs_lock_storage is not re-entrant (the inner wrap deadlocked
    every mutation with a 15 s "got lock request timeout"). The
    current release only wraps the three snapshot methods.

 -- TrueNAS Proxmox Plugin Maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Thu, 07 Aug 2026 15:00:00 +0000

truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.22+deb1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Fix pool.dataset.create crash on TrueNAS 25.10.4 (#58, #65, #78).
    Both create call sites (_tn_dataset_create and alloc_image's inline
    payload) omitted six optional fields: volblocksize (when
    tn_zvol_blocksize was unset), snapdev, reservation, refreservation,
    special_small_block_size, force_size. TrueNAS 25.10.4's legacy API
    shim leaves omitted optional fields as unresolved _NotRequired
    sentinel objects instead of real defaults, which crashes
    pool.dataset.create both during validation (dataset.py's
    __common_validation and do_create) and, even when validation
    passes, during audit-log JSON serialization afterward - the latter
    masks a create that actually succeeded server-side, leaving an
    orphaned zvol while Proxmox reports total failure. All six fields
    are now sent explicitly at both call sites. special_small_block_size
    is set to 'INHERIT' specifically: 0 fails a ZFS-level check ("does
    not apply to datasets of this type"), null fails the Pydantic
    schema check, INHERIT satisfies both, consistent with how every
    other inheritable property in the payload is already handled.
  * Fix tainted volsize/size values causing full clone and move-disk
    to fail under Perl taint mode (#71). _normalize_value, the
    common helper used to pull byte-count fields (volsize,
    volblocksize, available, quota, written, used) out of TrueNAS
    API responses, passed the decoded JSON scalar straight through
    without untainting it. Every value decoded from a WebSocket/
    broker socket read is tainted under Perl's -T mode, which
    pveproxy/pvedaemon run under. When PVE core called
    volume_size_info during a full clone or move-disk to a
    non-TrueNAS storage (NFS, dir, LVM, etc.) and interpolated the
    tainted size into the qemu-img create argv, the operation died
    with "Insecure dependency in exec while running with -T switch".
    _normalize_value now untaints the value via regex capture and
    dies loudly if a value is ever non-numeric, instead of silently
    forwarding a tainted or malformed scalar.

